  "title": "German Chancellor Merz Faces Disasters in State Elections",
  "summary": "German Chancellor Merz faces heavy losses in state elections, with the centre-right CDU party narrowly defeated, while the far-right AfD party gains significant support in Saxony-Anhalt, and leftwing parties aim to recover.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Friedrich Merz's CDU party narrowly lost 4.9% in Mecklenburg-Vorpommern, below the 5% threshold needed to enter parliament.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The AfD party won 41% in Saxony-Anhalt, marking a historic result, but remains uncertain about forming a government.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The CDU party's defeat highlights ongoing political fragmentation and the risk of radicalization.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
